ayenne pepper]]\n* 2 tbsp dried [[Cookbook:Dill|dill weed]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Garlic Powder|garlic powder]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Onion Powder|onion powder]]\n* 3 tbsp salt\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Paprika|paprika]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Black Pepper|black pepper]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] ground [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n* [[Cookbook:Lemon|Lemon]] [[Cookbook:Zest|zest]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Pound|pound]] (450 g) purged live [[Cookbook:Crawfish|craw/crayfish]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Bring water to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] in a stockpot or your tallest pot. Stir in seasonings.\n#Add crawfish, making sure to leave any dead ones behind. Cook for 7 minutes.\n#Turn off the heat and leave on the burner for 8 minutes. This allows the crawfish to soak in and absorb the flavorful broth without overcooking.\n#Drain through a [[Cookbook:Colander|colander]] and serve.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using crayfish]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Louisiana recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dill]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon zest]]\n[[Category:Pescatarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Halal recipes]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Crawfish Boil","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"½ gallon (2 liters) water","sourceText":"½ gallon (2 liters) water","amountText":"½ gallon (2 liters) water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 tbsp cayenne pepper","sourceText":"2 tbsp cayenne pepper","amountText":"2 tbsp cayenne pepper","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 tbsp dried dill weed","sourceText":"2 tbsp dried dill weed","amountText":"2 tbsp dried dill weed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 tbsp garlic powder","sourceText":"2 tbsp garlic pow